 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbW9B7SNHZ3/",
 "title": "10 Types of Bosses and How to Work With Each",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "This post explains ten different management styles and provides strategies for how employees can adapt to and work effectively with each type of boss. The main lesson is that managing your manager is a skill rather than a betrayal.",
 "key_points": [
  "The micromanager: Over-communicate before they ask to fill the info gap and loosen their grip.",
  "The absent boss: Set your own direction, update them, manage up, and do not wait to be managed.",
  "The visionary: Big on ideas and light on details; be the one who turns their vision into a plan.",
  "The conflict-avoider: Will not give hard feedback; ask for it directly and make it safe to be honest.",
  "The credit-taker: Document your work and share wins widely so your contribution is visible beyond them.",
  "The overwhelmed boss: Reduce their load instead of adding to it; bring solutions, not more problems.",
  "The perfectionist: Clarify the standard upfront so you are not endlessly redoing work.",
  "The friend-boss: Enjoy it, but keep it professional because blurred lines get awkward at review time.",
  "The data-driven one: Bring numbers, not vibes; speak their language to win them over fast.",
  "The insecure boss: Make them look good and never threaten them publicly; loyalty earns you room."
 ],
 "content": "Instagram reel/post by Anmol Bondada Venkata. Text / caption: You can’t pick your boss, but you can adapt. 10 boss types and how to handle each. 1. The micromanager. Over-communicate before they ask. Fill the info gap and they’ll loosen the grip. 2. The absent boss. Set your own direction and update them. Manage up, don’t wait to be managed. 3. The visionary. Big on ideas, light on details. Be the one who turns their vision into a plan. 4. The conflict-avoider. Won’t give hard feedback. Ask for it directly and make it safe to be honest. 5. The credit-taker. Document your work and share wins widely, so your contribution is visible beyond them. 6. The overwhelmed boss. Reduce their load, don’t add to it. Bring solutions, not more problems. 7. The perfectionist. Clarify the standard upfront so you’re not endlessly redoing work. 8. The friend-boss. Enjoy it, but keep it professional. Blurred lines get awkward at review time. 9. The data-driven one. Bring numbers, not vibes. Speak their language and you’ll win them fast. 10. The insecure boss. Make them look good and never threaten them publicly. Loyalty earns you room. Remember, managing your manager is a skill. Not a betrayal. Which one are you working with? [bosses, managers, career advice, leadership, corporate, managing up, career ladder, tech, global tech, American tech, work life, mnc life, skills, career tok, growth, explore] #managingup #manager #bosses #careeradvice #worktok. Text shown on screen: 10 types of bosses and how to work with each.",
